.idea/
.claude/
.superpowers/

node_modules/
out/
dist-installer/

# docs/ is handled as a whitelist. Everything else there is design and planning notes that stay
# local — written this way round so a new note defaults to "not published".
docs/*
!docs/releasing.md
!docs/slack-bot-setup.md
!docs/jobs.md
# Published deliberately: the SignPath Foundation requires the code signing policy to be reachable at
# a public URL, and the README links to it.
!docs/code-signing.md
# Not a note but an input: scripts/build-release-notes.cjs reads docs/release-notes/<tag>.md out of
# the checkout the publish job makes at the tag, so a write-up that is not committed does not exist.
!docs/release-notes/

# The source brand sheet (a 1254x1254 mockup). Icons are cropped from it and only the outputs are
# committed — see scripts/gen-icon.ps1.
astera.png
